<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech stats bureau revises 1997 economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>Czech stats bureau revises 1997 economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) on Friday revised its real 1997 GDP growth forecast to 2.9-3.5 percent, year-on-year, from a previous estimate of 4.0-5.0 percent.</p>
<p>The CSU added in a statement that it had revised its 1997 inflation forecast upward to 8.2-8.8 percent from 7.5-8.0 percent, its 1997 real industrial output estimate to 3.0-5.0 percent, its 1997 trade deficit forecast to 190-200 billion crowns from 202-212 billion.</p>
<p>It also revised its nominal wage growth forecast in 1997 to 14.0-15.5 from a previous estimate of 14.5-16.5 percent, year-on-year.</p>
</text>
